    "fileId": 16622,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Frequency of MAPK alterations detected to date in high-grade astrocytoma with piloid features</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "David Capper",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.35pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Type of MAPK alteration</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: right;\" align=\"right\"><strong>Frequency</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>NF1</em> mutation<sup>a</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: right;\" align=\"right\">19%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>NF1</em> heterozygous deletion<sup>a</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: right;\" align=\"right\">12%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>KIAA1549</em>::<em>BRAF</em> fusion</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: right;\" align=\"right\">20%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>BRAF</em> p.V600E mutation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: right;\" align=\"right\">1%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>FGFR1</em> p.K656E/N or p.N546D/K mutation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: right;\" align=\"right\">17%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>FGFR1</em>::<em>TACC1</em> fusion</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: right;\" align=\"right\">2%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 269.35pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"359\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>KRAS</em> mutation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: right;\" align=\"right\">3%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Three cases had both an <em>NF1</em> mutation and an <em>NF1</em> heterozygous deletion.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Data from Reinhardt et al. <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{29564591}</span>.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 40301,
    "bookid": 45,
